\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The voltage trace is one coordinate}
\date{2026-11-25}

\p{Let #{x} be a [trajectory](fnip-0009), and write
#{\varphi^{t}(x_{0})} for the point #{x(t)}. Its voltage trace is
the voltage coordinate of that point. In the Morris–Lecar pair of
\ref{fnip-0005} that coordinate is #{V}, so the trace is the function
#{t\mapsto V(t)}. The trajectory itself is the pair
#{(V(t),n(t))}.}

\p{At one fixed time, one value of #{V} belongs to many pairs, so the
function #{t\mapsto V(t)} does not determine the pair.}
